Z||000018||Songman||05-31-2001||07:57 PM||||Any club, group, or any other membership driven organization has some sort of set rules for being a part of it. Those rules are set up by the governing body or person. In the case of Kerri's website, it is Kerri. It is her website! She don't have to share it with anybody.<P>It's sorta like our TN Fiero Group. There are no membership fees or anything like that. You gotta do two things to join though. One is own a Fiero, and two is contact me telling me you want in. That is my set policy on joining. I do this to try to encourage people to get involved since we are new. In time, if we get a good thing going that is worth paying for there may be a fee. I certainly don't look down on any other club because they do charge a fee. They aren't being selfish. It is just how they do it...<P>And you do have to meet the requirements even here at good ole Pennock's Fiero Forum. You gotta have a computer, and e-mail address, and you gotta fill out that registration form. Lots of people hate registration forms! But it is worth it to be here...<P>Much like Kerri's site.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon12.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
